## Why This Is Asked
Real-world needs balance cost, latency, and reliability across tenants. This asks for a concrete policy language, a routing strategy, and test plans under varying traffic. It also probes drift handling and failover.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant QoS policies
- Multi-model routing with cost/latency prediction
- Data locality and failover strategies
- Observability: audit logs, drift tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing sketch
function route(req, tenant) {
  const p = policy[tenant];
  const candidates = models.filter(m => p.preferredModels.includes(m.name));
  // pick cheapest that meets latency
  return candidates
    .map(m => ({m, est: predict(m, req)}))
    .filter(x => x.est.lat <= p.max_latency)
    .sort((a,b) => a.est.cost - b.est.cost)[0]?.m;
}
```

